; %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
; UV-VIS ABSORPTION CROSS SECTIONS OF GLYOXAL AT 296K AND 1atm MEASURED WITH FTS AT 0.1nm FWHM
; %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
; 
; Experimental conditions:
; 
; - Mixtures of glyoxal and N2.
; - Static mode, pressure:  range 0.4 to 13.4 mbar of glyoxal in 1 atm N2.
; - Room temperature: 296K
; 
; Spectroscopic conditions
; 
; - Analysis light source: Xenon arc lamp(UV-VIS) / globar lamp (IR).
; - Detection system: 
; - Fourier Transform Spectrometer (Brucker IFS-120 HR)
; - Resolution: 0.1nm
; - Reaction vessel: glass, 83.5 cm, multi path optics (White type), mirrors: Al, path length 1.64 cm
; 
; Analysis
; 
; -Amount of glyoxal determined by converting pressure variation in an empty vessel into concentration. 1 atm N2 was added after pressure variation measurement.
; -Cell leak rate was and glyoxal losses were characterised and the glyoxal pressure was accordingly corrected 
; -Lamp drift characterised and corrected.
; -the combination of all remaining error sources yields an overall error which is 5% or better, but not less than 2?10-22 cm²/molec.
; 
; Absolute scaling
; 
; -Lambert-Beer Law.
; 
; Published:
; 
; UV/vis absorption cross section of Glyoxal
; Authors: Volkamer R; Spietz P; Burrows J; Platt U. ;
; title: High-resolution absorption cross-section of Glyoxal in the UV/vis and IR spectral ranges;
; quotation: J. Photochem. Photobiol. (2005) 172, 35. DOI: 10.1016/j.jphotochem.2004.11.011           
; 
; ----------------------------------------
; lambdaAir: air wavelength (nm)
; sigma: absorption cross sections (cm²)
; ----------------------------------------
